  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Zhen Wu blessed land, Yuan tribe headquarters in Northern Plains, a white robed first supreme elder practices spear methods above a peak pond while true martial carps criticize his form through Human Language. He holds rank seven with peak battle strength, and Yuan Chi reminds him that today is the day of the auction, so he collects Human Language and flies out.",
      "chapters": [
        747
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_zhen_wu_blessed_land",
        "fac_yuan_tribe",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "gu_human_language"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is a white robed old man with white hair, still greatly spirited, practicing spear work in the air above a peak pond.",
      "chapters": [
        747
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He enters the auction hall as Yuan tribe’s first supreme elder, still a rank seven Gu Immortal and leader of that Northern Plains super force, with battle strength and wealth that mark him as a strong bidder. He tells Qin Bai Sheng not to call him lord and to use the name Yuan Rang Zun, recalls an earlier fight that earned Qin Bai Sheng his acknowledgment, and asks for another spar after recent spear practice before taking a single room.",
      "chapters": [
        748
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "bai-sheng-auction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_qin_bai_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He stays in the late bidding for the mortal luck inspection Gu recipe among other large-force leaders.",
      "chapters": [
        760
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "bai-sheng-auction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_luck_inspection_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For the Red Fiend Divine Boat recipe he offers a wood path Immortal Gu and three hundred true martial carps, then hesitates over selling all the carps because Yuan tribe already holds an Immortal Gu House and drops out after Chanyu tribe leaves.",
      "chapters": [
        762
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "bai-sheng-auction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_red_fiend_divine_boat",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "fac_chanyu_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qin Bai Sheng lists a draw with Yuan Rang Zun among the fights that built his own Northern Plains fame as a lone cultivator.",
      "chapters": [
        766
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-and-reputation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Northern Plains Gu Immortals arrive to join Southern Border forces against Heavenly Court, Spear Deity Yuan Rang Zun is among the elites who follow Yao Huang, Heavenly Lord Bai Zu, and Prince Feng Xian, beside Domination Immortal Chu Du and others.",
      "chapters": [
        1727
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
